        "nl-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "203e152a-880e-37bb-a836-4e4d4850dad8",
                "word": "scheurbuik",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e5e9fcdf-7ddb-3869-92ba-26732040ee97",
                        "entry_id": "203e152a-880e-37bb-a836-4e4d4850dad8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "ziekte die vroeger veel voorkwam bij zeevarenden, veroorzaakt door een ernstig en langdurig tekort aan vitamine C (ascorbinezuur), zich o.a. kenmerkend door bloedend gezwollen tandvlees, blauwe vlekken, bloeding van huid en slijmvliezen en extreme zwakte."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "81c97956-2f24-49d2-9077-eab95045b22f",
                        "source_entry_id": "203e152a-880e-37bb-a836-4e4d4850dad8",
                        "source_sense_id": "e5e9fcdf-7ddb-3869-92ba-26732040ee97",
                        "source_sense_description": "ziekte ten gevolge van ascorbinezuurdeficiëntie",
                        "target_lang_word": "Skorbut",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Skorbut",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "caf02cd8-e22b-3edf-8802-0f5d6a7fc0f6",
                                        "entry_id": "a4a42586-396e-3180-b176-c57bb1dc5745",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Krankheit, die durch einen Mangel an Vitamin C hervorgerufen wird"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0716d08d-123e-41d3-90c5-107e2c8dfb72",
                                                "sense_id": "caf02cd8-e22b-3edf-8802-0f5d6a7fc0f6",
                                                "text": "In der Vergangenheit fielen viele Seeleute dem Skorbut zum Opfer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6de95a5c-634f-4768-8174-744950f5f25a",
                                                "sense_id": "caf02cd8-e22b-3edf-8802-0f5d6a7fc0f6",
                                                "text": "Um dem Skorbut vorzubeugen, hatte man Sauerkraut oder Zitronen an Bord von Schiffen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b8a94ac-b302-4194-b7ac-e08be86f846a",
                                                "sense_id": "caf02cd8-e22b-3edf-8802-0f5d6a7fc0f6",
                                                "text": "„Er tat dies aber, als fünf Tage später ein weiterer Gefangener starb, und zwar an Skorbut, wie er schrieb.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a51a1236-4a0b-4343-a448-1c800f27d6dd",
                                                "sense_id": "caf02cd8-e22b-3edf-8802-0f5d6a7fc0f6",
                                                "text": "„Trotzdem wäre es gefährlich, dieses Seemannsgarn – über Meerjungfrauen, Seeungeheuer und den ganzen Rest – zu belächeln und komisch zu finden, denn die Furcht vor diesen Dingen kann sich unter Deck wie eine Seuche ausbreiten und eine gute Crew schneller verderben als Skorbut.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48f57fee-5d8f-427c-8784-0f5724b2d133",
                                                "sense_id": "caf02cd8-e22b-3edf-8802-0f5d6a7fc0f6",
                                                "text": "„Die anderen erlitten Schiffbruch und ertranken, sie starben während der Überfahrt an Skorbut oder danach an tropischen Krankheiten.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70e0c923-64b7-4304-8472-b13a3bb6a71d",
                                                "sense_id": "caf02cd8-e22b-3edf-8802-0f5d6a7fc0f6",
                                                "text": "„Den Menschen drohten Mangelkrankheiten, zum Beispiel der Skorbut, weil man vom Eingemachten lebte und es frisches Obst oder Gemüse nicht gab.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "74629eb8-d839-47c9-808e-68c4c8ef47a9",
                        "source_entry_id": "203e152a-880e-37bb-a836-4e4d4850dad8",
                        "source_sense_id": "e5e9fcdf-7ddb-3869-92ba-26732040ee97",
                        "source_sense_description": "ziekte ten gevolge van ascorbinezuurdeficiëntie",
                        "target_lang_word": "scurvy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "scurvy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "18ff792f-9f52-3eb4-b9d1-36b5a810463a",
                                        "entry_id": "19275d8d-30d5-3d72-a4b1-d81198e3e3d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Affected or covered with scurf (“skin disease causing flakes of skin to fall off”) or scabs; scurfy, scabby; also, of or relating to a skin disease causing scurf or to scurvy (noun sense 1)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a932007d-0634-40ca-a5e7-ee3798675099",
                                                "sense_id": "18ff792f-9f52-3eb4-b9d1-36b5a810463a",
                                                "text": "Some wenches come vnlased, / Some hyswyues come vnbrased, / Wyth theyr naked pappes, / That flappes and flappes; / […] / A sorte of foule drabbes / All scuruy with scabbes: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b36cae44-e87b-4a37-bc70-88a6f5b4a690",
                                                "sense_id": "18ff792f-9f52-3eb4-b9d1-36b5a810463a",
                                                "text": "The bran of VVheate boiled in ſharpe vineger, and rubbed vpon them that be ſcuruie and mangie, easeth the partie very much."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f3b2790-8dc1-49c3-8093-f5cb9be66f2b",
                                                "sense_id": "18ff792f-9f52-3eb4-b9d1-36b5a810463a",
                                                "text": "This medicine is vvell approued to cure all ſorts of Paine, Scratches, Moully heeles, or any other skiruy ſcalls vvhatſoeuer, that may breede in a horſes leg or heeles, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d1dea58-aa36-4b89-b69c-f56aa08a2802",
                                                "sense_id": "18ff792f-9f52-3eb4-b9d1-36b5a810463a",
                                                "text": "Whoſoeuer he be of thy ſeed in their generations, that hath any blemiſh, let him not approche to offer the bread of his God: […] [he] that hath a blemiſh in his eye, or be ſcuruy, or ſcabbed, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b8a0ac15-7101-3d12-8521-1c98e413df7a",
                                        "entry_id": "19275d8d-30d5-3d72-a4b1-d81198e3e3d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of growths on plants: resembling scurf; scurfy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "478a3ab7-bf8a-36e4-a6e3-a8070c01b2cb",
                                        "entry_id": "19275d8d-30d5-3d72-a4b1-d81198e3e3d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a person or thing: disgustingly mean; contemptible, despicable, low."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0fd6c881-5fcd-4528-b943-822e87932554",
                                                "sense_id": "478a3ab7-bf8a-36e4-a6e3-a8070c01b2cb",
                                                "text": "a scurvy knave    a scurvy trick"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7eaa1d83-26a0-4a55-a93c-ba98779331c5",
                                                "sense_id": "478a3ab7-bf8a-36e4-a6e3-a8070c01b2cb",
                                                "text": "Iſt not a ſcuruie ieſt, that a man ſhould ieſt himſelfe to death."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2888bdb6-6197-4323-a06c-0ef95b395bd6",
                                                "sense_id": "478a3ab7-bf8a-36e4-a6e3-a8070c01b2cb",
                                                "text": "The Moore's abus'd by ſome outragious knaue: / Some baſe notorious knaue, some ſcuruy fellovv, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ff4086f-5dc7-4595-bfe4-b312e26da24b",
                                                "sense_id": "478a3ab7-bf8a-36e4-a6e3-a8070c01b2cb",
                                                "text": "VVhat a py'd Ninnie's this? Thou ſcuruy patch: / I do beſeech thy Greatneſſe giue him blovves, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f27178c4-0de3-402e-85fc-4b5d97714255",
                                                "sense_id": "478a3ab7-bf8a-36e4-a6e3-a8070c01b2cb",
                                                "text": "Hovv ſcuruy provvd he vvould looke, vvhen the Treaſury vvas full: / VVell, let him goe: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a2a4815-eeea-4a3e-a953-1478d96ce99f",
                                                "sense_id": "478a3ab7-bf8a-36e4-a6e3-a8070c01b2cb",
                                                "text": "And among other Regulations it vvould be very convenient to prevent the Exceſs of Drink, vvith that ſcurvy Cuſtom among the Lads, and Parent of the former Vice, the taking of Tobacco, vvhere it is not abſolutely neceſſary in Point of Health."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ad3591e-e6d9-480f-b319-a983af23f0e9",
                                                "sense_id": "478a3ab7-bf8a-36e4-a6e3-a8070c01b2cb",
                                                "text": "[W]e only had a scurvy dinner at an alehouse, and he made me go to the tavern, and drink Florence, four and sixpence a flask; damned wine?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89836cfc-2779-4e03-bac6-0b8ac07efb8b",
                                                "sense_id": "478a3ab7-bf8a-36e4-a6e3-a8070c01b2cb",
                                                "text": "[T]he company here vvere not ſo riotous as the Bucks of Covent-Garden, but formed themſelves into a circle, vvithin vvhich ſome of the number danced to the muſick of a ſcurvy organ and a fevv other inſtruments, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19be8ccd-6c21-4a77-8934-602ed2b4faee",
                                                "sense_id": "478a3ab7-bf8a-36e4-a6e3-a8070c01b2cb",
                                                "text": "I have a scurvy touch of old puritanical humour about me. I abide not the imposition of hands—take off your grasp from my cloak, or I will find means to make you unloose it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3d121847-f9eb-3847-971a-c2537ae3a43d",
                                        "entry_id": "19275d8d-30d5-3d72-a4b1-d81198e3e3d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of the way someone is treated: poor, shabby."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "scurvy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2dbcf8c6-6d54-3546-af25-0d16f67aa8b7",
                                        "entry_id": "bcb81a1c-6c47-3bb0-9445-ef3fae305776",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A disease caused by insufficient intake of vitamin C, leading to the formation of livid spots on the skin, spongy gums, loosening of the teeth, and bleeding into the skin and from almost all mucous membranes; (countable, obsolete) an occurrence of this disease."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "885ecd33-ae97-4d44-8324-d63fe695493a",
                                                "sense_id": "2dbcf8c6-6d54-3546-af25-0d16f67aa8b7",
                                                "text": "Our legs now vs deceiue, / ſwolne euery ioint withall, / With this diſeaſe, which, by your leaue, / the Scuruie men doe call."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "39840745-7fb8-43f4-b975-5576eb06532a",
                                                "sense_id": "2dbcf8c6-6d54-3546-af25-0d16f67aa8b7",
                                                "text": "[H]ee will go to the ſea, and teare the gold out of the Spaniards throats but he will haue it, byrlady when he comes there, poore ſoule hee lyes in brine in Baliſt, and is lamentable ſicke of the ſcuruies; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af561be0-89dc-4437-a66c-11cd3ee0c734",
                                                "sense_id": "2dbcf8c6-6d54-3546-af25-0d16f67aa8b7",
                                                "text": "[W]hich excellent plant [scurvy-grass], Cæſars ſoldiers […] found to preuaile […] againſt that plague and hurtfull diſeaſe of the teeth, gums, and ſinevves, called the Scuruie, being a depriuation of all good bloode and moiſture, in the vvhole bodie, called Scorbutum; in Engliſh the Scuruie, and Skyrbie: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4962c193-f7be-4b56-a0d3-479cd5143b65",
                                                "sense_id": "2dbcf8c6-6d54-3546-af25-0d16f67aa8b7",
                                                "text": "[N]ovv vve have looſed the plough in the fields, they'l find vvork enough about home to keep us from the ſcurvey."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7508542c-d8fd-4804-a074-5a87584b1c79",
                                                "sense_id": "2dbcf8c6-6d54-3546-af25-0d16f67aa8b7",
                                                "text": "The Scurvies is the Mother and Nurſery of all Diſeaſes: and upon taking old, or any diſorder of Body, they branch out one Diſtemper or other, and yet the grand cauſe, vvhich is the Scurvies, remains all in one Body."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "836a9b53-1020-4649-ace9-cd96c9cfba92",
                                                "sense_id": "2dbcf8c6-6d54-3546-af25-0d16f67aa8b7",
                                                "text": "But I muſt allovv that this VVater is moſt indovv'd vvith theſe Acid Streams by this means, and may repute it as moſt Medicinal in Scurvies, on the Score of the Quantity of Acid, Chalybeat, and Allummy, extraordinary in this."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "498953b8-4960-4d4a-aaeb-24fd0676108f",
                                                "sense_id": "2dbcf8c6-6d54-3546-af25-0d16f67aa8b7",
                                                "text": "Native Animal Oils, as Fat, Cream, Butter, Marrovv, eſpecially the laſt, vvhich is excellent in ſome Scurvies."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51623161-9a89-49de-81af-e3c27f48e3ae",
                                                "sense_id": "2dbcf8c6-6d54-3546-af25-0d16f67aa8b7",
                                                "text": "And then as to your ſcurvys, and gouts, rheumatiſms, conſumptions, coughs and catarrhs, tar-vvater and turpentine vvill make you as ſound as a roach."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f578aad-0b50-44cc-9268-95579a1118f2",
                                                "sense_id": "2dbcf8c6-6d54-3546-af25-0d16f67aa8b7",
                                                "text": "The chief use, however, of the fresh provisions was for the men with the scurvy. One of them was able to eat, and he soon brought himself to by gnawing upon raw potatoes; but the other, by this time, was hardly able to open his mouth; and the cook took the potatoes raw, pounded them in a mortar, and gave him the juice to drink."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e8c13ee-c1cd-456f-a821-e380633c5074",
                                                "sense_id": "2dbcf8c6-6d54-3546-af25-0d16f67aa8b7",
                                                "text": "Conditions were horrendous aboard most British naval vessels at the time. Scurvy and other diseases ran rampant, killing more seamen each year than all other causes combined, including combat."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3b4e4f09-0ab6-30f2-a80b-5ebe4912bcac",
                                        "entry_id": "bcb81a1c-6c47-3bb0-9445-ef3fae305776",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A contemptible or despicable person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f9630222-7a6d-4f27-8085-3c56e914bd06",
                                                "sense_id": "3b4e4f09-0ab6-30f2-a80b-5ebe4912bcac",
                                                "text": "Row, row you scurvies, / She'll have us boiled in oil. / Move, move those creaking oars, / until you reach Cape soil."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a518eef9-860f-4f11-921f-6b144c91f2a1",
                                                "sense_id": "3b4e4f09-0ab6-30f2-a80b-5ebe4912bcac",
                                                "text": "Muppet Treasure Island (1996) Avast! There be no treasure on this island, just a bunch of googly-eyed, synthetic scurvies staging a bastardized retelling of the classic Robert Louis Stevenson adventure."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef69a6fe-171f-4053-aba5-ca71c33057a8",
                                                "sense_id": "3b4e4f09-0ab6-30f2-a80b-5ebe4912bcac",
                                                "text": "Her friends kept writing her warning her that the man market was not that fortuitous, and filled [with] wormies, and scurvies, unctuous bedfellows that would make her chin jut out— […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "032e7b93-a66e-3ba1-8b6c-9d53563ac4ca",
                                        "entry_id": "bcb81a1c-6c47-3bb0-9445-ef3fae305776",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A cattle disease, perhaps affecting the skin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b74d819c-70c2-4b6c-8514-d6c881a7503d",
                        "source_entry_id": "203e152a-880e-37bb-a836-4e4d4850dad8",
                        "source_sense_id": "e5e9fcdf-7ddb-3869-92ba-26732040ee97",
                        "source_sense_description": "ziekte ten gevolge van ascorbinezuurdeficiëntie",
                        "target_lang_word": "scorbut",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "scorbut",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d08d3434-b3ad-3733-a9fd-60bd4888d3a9",
                                        "entry_id": "30b9d75b-c0cd-3d0a-b54b-9691368ca476",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Maladie générale caractérisée par des hémorragies, des troubles gastro-intestinaux, des gencives attaquées, l’affaiblissement progressif puis la consomption, et due à un manque de vitamine C nécessaire à la synthèse du collagène (avitaminose C)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Nosologie"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1cd3b100-d20f-4af2-8fef-0362d2be1281",
                                                "sense_id": "d08d3434-b3ad-3733-a9fd-60bd4888d3a9",
                                                "text": "Nous manquions d’eau, et une grande partie de l’équipage était attaquée par le scorbut : il fut décidé que nous relâcherions à Rio-Janéiro."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a27f4fa2-d011-4604-92f7-3596d12a7824",
                                                "sense_id": "d08d3434-b3ad-3733-a9fd-60bd4888d3a9",
                                                "text": "Du reste, aucun symptôme de scorbut ne s’était encore manifesté parmi les habitants du Fort-Espérance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e04fda7b-4e43-4b1e-9558-a95a73618416",
                                                "sense_id": "d08d3434-b3ad-3733-a9fd-60bd4888d3a9",
                                                "text": "La découverte de l’effet des agrumes sur la maladie du scorbut remonte au XVIᵉ siècle. Dès lors, avant d’entreprendre une longue traversée, les marins embarquèrent des provisions d’oranges et de citrons. L’acide ascorbique contenu dans ces fruits prendra le nom de vitamine C en 1932."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d93789f-4a64-46b8-98ad-6daf0263b515",
                                                "sense_id": "d08d3434-b3ad-3733-a9fd-60bd4888d3a9",
                                                "text": "C'est une maladie d'une autre époque : celle des explorateurs et des marins. Le scorbut est rarissime au Québec de nos jours et, pourtant, deux cas ont été traités à Montréal en un mois seulement. Un type de carence potentiellement exacerbé par la pandémie."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
